    "narrative": "As we approach the final stretch of the 2026 season, Ghost Ride the WHIP leans heavily into speed and favorable matchups for today\u2019s card. The standout play is **Corbin Carroll** (76.39), who benefits from a prime matchup against Rocker. His dynamic platoon advantage and current form make him our highest-projected asset, closely followed by **Trevor Story** (70.65) and **James Wood** (70.43). **James Wood** is particularly compelling today; occupying the leadoff spot against Ure\u00f1a, his elite .415 xwOBA suggests he is the primary catalyst for our run production. Meanwhile, **Brice Turang** earns a strong recommendation at 69.44, as his presence in the #2 hole against Singer provides the necessary volume and stolen base upside that anchors our 5x5 strategy.\n\nOur most difficult sit-start decision involved **Griffin Conine**, who missed the 40-point efficiency floor by a razor-thin margin (39.71). While **Griffin Conine** holds upside, the high-skill profile of Glasnow necessitated a benching to preserve our game caps. Similarly, **Travis Bazzana** and **Isaac Paredes** fell short of the threshold, with **Isaac Paredes** specifically hampered by an unfavorable L/L platoon disadvantage against Seymour. On the defensive side of our roster, **Austin Riley** remains a marginal start (42.15); while his raw talent is undeniable, the encounter with a sharp Mayza suppresses his ceiling, making him our riskiest active play. Monitor **Vinnie Pasquantino** closely as well; despite his favorable park adjustment, his score of 50.49 is heavily impacted by a harsh 15% penalty due to the platoon split against Suarez. We are currently holding **Jose Caballero** on the pine as he is absent from today's active lineup, leaving our core of **Gabriel Moreno**, **Josh Naylor**, and **Cole Young** to carry the weight of our daily efficiency goals.",
